<br><HTML>Just a word to everyone.  I can make fine plate now.  I am willing to make it AT COST for anyone in the guild.  You will be responsible for paying for the materials, and any failures.  My smithing is at 180, so bracers/collars/visors are easier to make than legs, cloaks, or breastplates.  Cost for materials really rises with the total number of MQ folded sheets I have to make which are required for the item and the molds.<br>
<br>
50pp/attempt (1 sheet) for visors, collars and bracers; <br>
75pp/attempt (2 sheets) for helms, pauldruns, girdles, vambraces, gauntlets, and boots; <br>
100pp/attempt (3 sheets) for breastplates, cloaks and greaves<br>
<br>
<br>
-Jiggs</HTML></font></tt><p>
