Author:&nbsp;<a href="/showmember.php?name=Jiggles">Jiggles</a>&nbsp;(---.roleplayers.org)<br>
Date:&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;03-06-01 01:18<br>
<br><HTML>I'll just say this here quickly before I go to sleep.  I'm not even going to attempt mithril until fine plate is trivial to me, Im level 49, and I'm rich.  I'm still at 180 smithing, and that goes trivial at 208.  I don't forsee that happening any time soon.  I'm also still level 30, and not fighting nearly as much as I should.<br>
<br>
Reason is this: to enchant mitrhil, you need a lvl 49 enchanter to make enchant a mithril block (which consumes a rare blue diamond as a casting cost for EACH block)  In addition, most items require more than one block, vials of swirling mist, essense of moonlight, etc for the tempur.  These items are supposedly never trivial, or they are up in the 250point range which means a 1/8 - 1/10 chance of success.<br>
<br>
Needless to say, to make ONE attempt at cost would be a few thousand platinum depending on what you want to make.  Unfortunately, the only people who could afford this are high level players, and most of them have already bought or twinked themselves with better equipment.  Verant made this smithing a bit too hard and that is why you just don't see very many people sporting smithed mithril chain or plate.  There are other mithril items out there, but those are dropped off monsters.<br>
<br>
-Jiggles</HTML></font></tt><p>
